# Local secrets for the TAI LEARNING OS Worker.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the values below. `.dev.vars` is
# gitignored and must never be committed: these are the credentials that let
# someone sign in as the parent and sign sessions, so they are exactly what the
# repository must not carry.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# Nothing in this file accesses a paid service or a remote database. The Worker
# is LOCAL ONLY in this MVP: it runs under `wrangler dev` against a local D1
# file, and no line of this configuration creates a Cloudflare resource.

# ── SESSION_SECRET ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs session tokens and derives the CSRF token. Must be high-entropy.
#
# The app refuses to serve ANY protected route when this is missing (see
# src/worker/http/middleware.ts): a missing secret must fail closed, never fall
# back to an unsigned or guessable default.
#
# Generate one:
#   node -e 'console.log(require("crypto").randomBytes(32).toString("base64url"))'
#
# Changing this value signs every existing parent out, which is the correct
# consequence of rotating a signing key.
SESSION_SECRET=

# ── PARENT_PASSWORD_HASH ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The parent's password, stored only as a PBKDF2-SHA256 hash. The app refuses to
# serve protected routes when this is missing UNLESS ENVIRONMENT is "development",
# which is what lets first-run account creation work on a fresh local database.
#
# Deliberately NOT a password: this file holds no plaintext credential. To make
# one from a password you choose:
#
#   npm run hash:password -- 'your-password-here'
#
# Keep the single quotes: an unquoted password in a shell history is a password
# in a file. Never reuse a password you use anywhere else — this app has no
# remote service to reset it for you.
#
# On a fresh local database you can leave this empty, create the parent account
# through the app's own bootstrap route, and then set it so subsequent runs
# require the password you chose.
PARENT_PASSWORD_HASH=
